  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mongolia: Judicial Engagement and Transparency (JET)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To strengthen relations between civil society organizations and the justice system actors to promote dialogue and collaboration in the context of the justice reform process. 2) To improve relations and communications between the media and justice actors.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Aimag/district courts, the Constitutional Court, the Judicial General Council, the Judicial Disciplinary Committee, the Ministry of Justice and Home Affairs, the National Legal Institute, the Media Council, the National Committee on Gender Equality, the Research and Training Institute of the Supreme Court, the Supreme Court, journalists, journalism and law faculties and students, judges and lawyers, and urban and rural civil society organizations in Mongolia.Indirect beneficiaries: Vulnerable communities, justice sector actors, and the population of Mongolia at large.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enhance the participation of civil society and the media in accountability of the justice system.</narrative>
  </description>
